<%# Replaces the old left panel, which spent 45% of every desktop screen on a
    logo and the hotel name and left the actual page squeezed into the rest.
    This says the same three things in one row and gives the width back.

    It carries the page's h1: the templates below it are all sections of one
    property's concierge, so their own headings stay h2. %>
<header class="sticky top-0 z-20 border-b border-border/60 bg-background/85 backdrop-blur-sm">
  <%# Two sizes. On a desktop the 32px chip sets the height, landing at 49px --
      under a tenth of the viewport even on a 600px-tall window. On a phone the
      vertical budget is the scarcest of all, so the bar drops to a bare label:
      no icon chip, no location line, tight leading -- about 12px, half of the
      already-reduced 25px. The guest is standing in the hotel; the name alone
      is enough to confirm whose concierge this is. %>
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between gap-4 px-3 py-[2px] sm:px-6 sm:py-2">
    <%= link_to concierge_home_path(@hotel), class: "group flex min-w-0 items-center gap-0 sm:gap-3" do %>
      <span class="hidden shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-foreground transition-transform group-active:scale-95 sm:flex sm:h-8 sm:w-8">
        <%= cached_icon "concierge-bell", class: "h-3.5 w-3.5" %>
      </span>
      <span class="min-w-0">
        <h1 class="truncate text-[9px] font-black leading-none text-foreground sm:text-[12px] sm:leading-tight"><%= @hotel.name %></h1>
        <p class="hidden truncate text-[9px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted-foreground sm:block">
          <%= concierge_location_label(@hotel) %>
        </p>
      </span>
    <% end %>

    <span class="hidden shrink-0 text-[9px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-muted-foreground/70 sm:block">
      Digital Concierge
    </span>
  </div>
</header>
